From ec713801c27eaa3783dac4eba4bd365d807b880c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JFIREonFIRE <100313949+JFIREonFIRE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:39:18 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Memory switches for 32 GB PCs, all off by default

- VICTORY_WAIT_RESIDENT=textures: only texture blocks and textures are made
  not resident and waited for; plain buffers skip MakeResident and the
  mapped() wait (#346).
- VICTORY_TEXTURE_KEEP_PERCENT=<p>: moves vram_keep's three lines down
  together (unset: 85/93, as before); every MB the card keeps is also commit.
- VICTORY_STAGING_BAR=1: texture staging blocks in resizable-BAR card memory
  while the card is under 85 % of its budget.
- VICTORY_PRESSURE_PHYSICAL=1: residency pressure by free physical memory
  alone (on at 1.5 GiB, off at 2.5 GiB), emergency commit floor 256 MiB.
- VICTORY_WINDOWS_BAR_PERCENT=<p>: how full the card may be for a window to
  go into its CPU-mapped memory (unset: 80, as before).

Measured on an RTX 3090 / 32 GB with the same code on a codec-d/cool_fox
based tree (#333, #346).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
